Description:
    The `trails new` command creates a new Trails application with a default
    directory structure and configuration at the path you specify.

    You can specify extra command-line arguments to be used every time
    `trails new` runs in the .trailsrc configuration file in your home directory,
    or in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/trails/trailsrc if XDG_CONFIG_HOME is set.

    Note that the arguments specified in the .trailsrc file don't affect the
    default values shown above in this help message.

Examples:
    `trails new ~/Code/TypeScript/weblog`

    This generates a new Trails app in ~/Code/TypeScript/weblog.

    `trails new weblog --api`

    This generates a new Trails app in API mode in ./weblog.

    `trails new weblog --skip-action-mailer`

    This generates a new Trails app without Action Mailer in ./weblog.
    Any part of Trails can be skipped during app generation.
